{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966802,"nonce":"8ix/hvOwOaswsD1K4Cl1Ti3lHGk=","title":"Stateful auto-registers a POINTER_DOWN-\u003eFocused FSM handler and event handlers APPEND","message":"`Stateful::ensure_state_handlers_registered` (stateful.rs) auto-registers POINTER_ENTER/LEAVE/DOWN/UP handlers that drive the FSM (`TextFieldState`: `(Idle|Hovered, POINTER_DOWN) =\u003e Focused`). `EventHandlers::on` APPENDS to a `Vec` per event type and `dispatch` calls ALL of them (event_handler.rs). So a widget's own `.on_mouse_down(...)` does NOT replace the auto handler — both fire, auto first (registered during `with_shared_state`, before the builder's `.on_mouse_down`).\n\nConsequence for text_input: the `:focus` outline ring is painted from the FSM `shared.state` (via the Stateful `state_callback`), NOT `data.visual`. Only the manual `on_mouse_down` path calls `set_focused_text_input` (updates the global `FOCUSED_TEXT_INPUT` tracker + blurs the previous). If that manual handler early-returns (e.g. `cn::input_otp` `on_focus_request` bounces focus to the first empty slot), the auto handler has ALREADY latched the clicked slot's FSM to Focused -\u003e it rings, but it's not in the global tracker, so `blur_all_text_inputs` (which only clears the single tracked input) can never reach it. Symptom: click each OTP slot -\u003e each keeps a ring; click outside -\u003e only the first (tracked) clears.\n\nFix (commit d7eb6356): `blur_text_input_deferred(state)` -\u003e `PENDING_BLUR_INPUT`, drained at the top of `process_pending_input_focus` (which runs after event dispatch). A SYNCHRONOUS blur from the OTP redirect no-ops because it runs before the auto handler within the same dispatch; deferring makes it run after, so it wins. The OTP `on_focus_request` redirect now defers a blur of the clicked slot. A public `blur_text_input(state)` (clear_focused_text_input + blur_text_input_state) is the single-slot blur `blur_all_text_inputs` lacks.\n\nPrereq that made the repaint land: `TextInput::from_config` used to wipe the reused stateful's `node_id = None` every rebuild; when the incremental diff skips an unchanged slot, `Stateful::build` never runs to restore it, so `refresh_props_internal` hit its `node_id == None` early-return and dropped the blur's repaint. Removed the wipe (`StatefulInner::new` already starts None; `build` overwrites whenever a rebuild runs). Same node_id-loss lesson as external-state changes not captured by the diff hash.\n\nTest blind spot: `focusing_future_empty_slot_redirects_to_first_empty_slot` checked `data.visual` (never set on the redirect path) so it passed regardless. The ring source is the FSM -\u003e assert `stateful_state.state.is_focused()`. See `redirected_click_does_not_leave_slot_fsm_focused`. Related: gotcha in place path skips classes and element type, gotcha stateful merge from missing fields.\n\n**Web runner never drained the deferred focus queue (commit bf577b8d).** `process_pending_input_focus` / `process_pending_area_focus` (which drain `PENDING_FOCUS_INPUT` / `PENDING_BLUR_INPUT`, the queues `focus_text_input_deferred` / `blur_text_input_deferred` fill) were called ONLY from `windowed.rs` (desktop), not `web.rs`. So on web, OTP auto-advance-per-keystroke, backspace-rewind, and the redirected-click blur silently no-opped (queued, never applied) — symptom: typing didn't move focus to the next slot, backspace stalled after the last couple slots. Fix: added a \"Phase 4c\" drain in `web.rs` `render()` after the rebuild phases (node_id set) and before the Phase 5 focus sync (so `:focus` reflects it same frame). When adding any new per-frame `process_pending_*` drain, wire it in BOTH `windowed.rs` and `web.rs` (and check `ios.rs`/`android.rs`).","files":null}]}